//
// @PLN153 phase 1 — the REFUSE half of @FR-N-Prop's pair: null rides through `+`, so the sum is τ? and a τ slot refuses it.
//
// The pair exists so the citation at the rule's home is a receipt for a measured
// refusal, not a comment: `rule_tags.py check` counts the citation, this file is what
// makes it honest.  Its expectation is the diagnostic's own text, pinned as a substring.
//
// @falsified-at: none — pins a refusal the compiler already makes; the negation cell of a
//   rule that holds, not a fix, so no earlier build is a control for it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot change type from integer to integer?
fn f(n: integer?) -> integer { m: integer = n + 5; return m; }
fn main() { println("{f(1)}"); }
